  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding from Alaska Medicaid Serostim Criteria Version 2. Last updated 4/15/2016; approved 4/29/2016; effective 10/3/2016.",
    "Encoded: closed HIV/AIDS wasting/cachexia indication, HIV infection, current ART, failure or contraindication to either Marinol or Megace, exclusion of other weight-loss causes, any of four weight-loss severity paths, either clinical syndrome path, and all additional denial exclusions. No numeric age gate is specified.",
    "Reauthorization (notes only): lean body mass and body weight must have increased and physical endurance improved due to Serostim. Deny if the rate of weight loss was unaffected (did not slow, stop, stabilize, or improve).",
    "Initial coverage up to 6 months; subsequent reauthorization up to 12 months. Duration and reauthorization require manual review.",
    "Quantity limit: None. Dosage forms: 4 mg, 5 mg, and 6 mg powder for injection.",
    "Mechanism of action (notes only): anabolic and anticatabolic effects through receptors on multiple cell types, including muscle, liver, fat, lymphocytes and hematopoietic cells; some effects are mediated by IGF-1.",
    "No evaluate()-linked alternatives: Egrifta treats excess abdominal fat in HIV lipodystrophy and is not indicated for weight loss management. Somatropin class criteria are not encoded by this pack."
  ],
